h falling to 12-22%. [Source: FMP /analyst-estimates] This reflects base effects compounding and natural questions about whether hyperscaler CapEx cycles can sustain current intensity into 2027-2028. The remaining performance obligation of only $1.9B [Source: SEC EDGAR XBRL, 2026 Q2] suggests most NVIDIA revenue is recognized on shipment with limited long-term contractual visibility — a meaningful data gap for multi-year modeling.\n\nThird, the ROA of 65.7% [Source: FMP /ratios-ttm] and D/E of 0.07 underscore a pristine balance sheet, but the $148.96M in recent insider sales, entirely sells with zero buys, adds a cautionary signal at current valuations, even if much of this is likely systematic plan-based selling. [Source: FMP /insider-transactions]\n\nThe DCF intrinsic value of $235.50 implies ~19% upside to current prices, suggesting the market has priced in robust but not heroic execution. With analyst consensus at $275.74 average target (38.9% upside), the street remains constructively positioned. At a $4.8T market cap, NVDA must sustain $130B+ annualized FCF to justify current multiples — achievable if AI infrastructure spending remains structurally elevated but exposed to any demand air pocket or competitive displacement risk.",
